WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.588
Let AI coding

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.085
agents loose safely

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:03.781
in a VM

00:00:04.302 --> 00:00:05.127
Hangar is a

00:00:04.939 --> 00:00:06.542
free open-source Mac

00:00:06.366 --> 00:00:07.486
app and CLI

00:00:07.297 --> 00:00:08.358
that runs Claude

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.384
Code and Codex

00:00:09.196 --> 00:00:10.610
inside a macOS

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:11.908
Linux or Windows

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:12.816
virtual machine

00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:14.568
With approvals off

00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:15.818
agents can't touch

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.726
your Mac's files

00:00:16.785 --> 00:00:18.200
your SSH or

00:00:18.012 --> 00:00:18.967
cloud keys

00:00:19.106 --> 00:00:19.942
They see only

00:00:19.754 --> 00:00:20.485
the folder you

00:00:20.297 --> 00:00:21.593
share and reach

00:00:21.535 --> 00:00:22.395
only the sites

00:00:22.207 --> 00:00:22.926
you allow

00:00:23.462 --> 00:00:24.393
And if one

00:00:24.205 --> 00:00:25.112
breaks something

00:00:25.184 --> 00:00:26.598
one command undoes

00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:27.506
everything it did

00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:28.624
Install it with

00:00:28.436 --> 00:00:29.166
Homebrew

00:00:29.694 --> 00:00:30.708
Full story on

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:31.415
the dashboard
